;**********************************************************************
; MZ header at file offsets 0000h..001Fh. File size 9280 bytes; 32-byte header, no relocations, 9248-byte load module.
; CS=SS=load_segment-0010h selects the PSP; entry PSP:0100h, SP=FFFEh. Minimum extra allocation 0DBEh paragraphs brings the
; rounded load plus allocation to 1000h paragraphs. Maximum FFFFh requests the largest available block.
;**********************************************************************
mz_magic:
0000:0000       4d5a                      word      5A4Dh
                ; The base view preserves the input. first_decode uses initial PSP offsets; body_plaintext_units uses offsets
; after CS=PSP+12h and independently decrypts 95 inline units. These units are not simultaneously plaintext at runtime. Separate
; code views resolve transition decoding, decoder templates and overlapping or patched instructions. Skipped byte objects are
; bounded by verified transfers and independently established neighboring entries; their historical purpose is not inferred. The
; seasonal payload recursively decodes its active body; key-dependent ciphertext paths include halting, malformed returns and
; memory overruns. Key-specific views explain execution under their stated keys and entry state. Calculations over captured RAM
; with substituted keys are static deductions, not captured execution; joint PIT-key and memory histories remain unproved.
; External inputs and interrupt or device state are conditional where identified. Instruction sequences assume synchronous
; execution unless interrupt delivery is explicitly discussed. Named EXTERNAL locations also describe runtime targets, including
; BIOS byte 0000:0475h and host-PSP words; those targets are explained at their accesses rather than added as memory blocks.
